---
/**
 * Proof.astro — Evidence-backed claims with real numbers + real refusal strings.
 */
---

<section class="section proof" id="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title" data-reveal-section>
  <div class="section-shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker reveal">Proof, not promises</p>
      <h2 id="proof-title" class="reveal">Every number measured. Every claim sourced.</h2>

    </div>

    <ul class="proof-list" data-proof-list>
      <li class="proof-item" data-proof-item>
        <b class="proof-stat proof-stat--accent">9</b>
        <span class="proof-label">Documented MCP paths</span>
      </li>
      <li class="proof-item" data-proof-item>
        <b class="proof-stat proof-stat--success">1</b>
        <span class="proof-label">Verified host (OpenCode 1.18.13)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="proof-item" data-proof-item>
        <b class="proof-stat proof-stat--neutral">0</b>
        <span class="proof-label">Provider credentials stored</span>
      </li>
      <li class="proof-item" data-proof-item>
        <b class="proof-stat proof-stat--neutral">0</b>
        <span class="proof-label">Runtime dependencies (stdlib + SQLite)</span>
      </li>
      <li class="proof-item" data-proof-item>
        <b class="proof-stat proof-stat--accent">1</b>
        <span class="proof-label">Coordinator node (single-node preview)</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="proof-note reveal">
      The next proof pair, Claude Code + Cursor, is what the design-partner cohort exists to produce.
    </p>
    <p class="proof-honest reveal">
      This is a single-node preview — one coordinator, one workspace, one honest boundary.
      Multi-node replication is on the roadmap.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
